70	\subsection{Speed-Estimation Bias}
71	The receiver-side speed estimate is $\hat v=v+\Delta v$, $\Delta v=b_v+\nu_v$, $\nu_v\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_v^2)$. A biased estimate perturbs both the Doppler-derived predictor coefficient and, more importantly here, the receiver's notion of coherence time. We analyze signed bias and show below that the sign matters: overestimating speed is conservative.
72	
73	\subsection{Performance Metrics}
74	For a pilot period $P$ (one pilot symbol every $P$ OFDM symbols), the $P{-}1$ data symbols use CSI at prediction horizons $1,\dots,P{-}1$. With pilot overhead $1/P$ and mean data-symbol BER $\bar b(P,v)$, we use the goodput, in useful bits per symbol,
75	\begin{equation}
76	G(P,v)=\Big(1-\tfrac{1}{P}\Big)\,\log_2(M_{\rm mod})\,\big(1-\bar b(P,v)\big),
77	\label{eq:goodput}
78	\end{equation}
79	which jointly captures the overhead/aging trade-off ($M_{\rm mod}=4$ for QPSK).
