174	\subsection{BER Is Governed by Horizon vs. Coherence}
175	Figure~\ref{fig:horizon} plots BER against the horizon. On sum-of-sinusoids Jakes, BER climbs from $0.009$ at $d=1$ to $0.45$ at $d=64$, tracking the correlation decay of Table~\ref{tab:corr}; on the AR(1) surrogate it barely moves (to $0.026$). Two conclusions follow: in the simulated setup the horizon rather than predictor refinement dominates detection quality; and a surrogate-based study would wrongly conclude that long-horizon prediction is safe.
