243	\subsection{Threshold Sensitivity}
244	The rule has a single design parameter, the correlation threshold $\rho_{\rm th}$. Figure~\ref{fig:rho} sweeps it and reports goodput averaged over $30$--$210$ km/h, together with the mean selected period. The trade-off is explicit: a low threshold ($0.80$) lets the period grow ($\bar P^\star\approx35$), saving overhead but operating near the coherence edge, whereas a high threshold ($0.98$) forces short periods ($\bar P^\star\approx13$) and pays excessive pilot overhead. Average goodput peaks at $\rho_{\rm th}=0.90$ ($1.826$ bits/symbol) and stays within $1\%$ over the broad range $[0.85,0.95]$, so performance is insensitive to the exact value and $\rho_{\rm th}=0.9$ is a robust default rather than a tuned constant.
